Analysis B3-B4 - Matched replicas and heterogeneity of IA-AG differences
========================================================================

Pre-specified definitions (fixed before any comparison was computed):
  margin occupancy_pax          = 2.0
  margin travel_time_s          = 10.0
  margin trip_duration_s        = 60.0
  margin flow_per_visit_pax     = 0.5
  margin wait_median_s          = 30.0
  margin wait_tail_s            = 60.0
  margin prob_pp                = 2.0
  margin denied_rel             = 0.1
  margin headway_cv             = 0.05
  empirical acceptance: Bhattacharyya coefficient >= 0.97 (project rule, data_extractor.py)
  empirical W1 tolerance: 2.0 passengers
  operational issue rule (D5): P(O >= 60) >= 0.10
  crowding threshold: 60 passengers (75 % of capacity 80)
  peak slots: (7, 8, 9, 17, 18, 19)
  bootstrap: 1000 resamples of complete replicas, seed 20261013
  equivalence: 95 % CI of the IA-AG difference inside +-margin -> EQUIVALENT;
               CI entirely outside -> NOT EQUIVALENT; otherwise INCONCLUSIVE


B3 - Matched-replica comparison
-------------------------------
Not applicable: each GAMA batch draws its own random stream per replica (the MASTER_SEED of the
pipeline is not used by GAMA and the two runs have different seeds), and IA consumes random numbers
in a different order (one draw per passenger agent). Replicas are therefore treated as independent
samples in every CI (independent bootstrap per model).

B4 - Heterogeneity of the IA-AG difference in mean occupancy (strata: direction x stop x departure slot)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Replica-bootstrap 95 % CI (500 resamples) of IA - AG per stratum; equivalence margin +-2.0 pax.
Demand tertiles from known_data mean occupancy (cut points 18.6 and 33.3 pax),
defined from the empirical reference, independently of the IA-AG comparison.
